+#### [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF)
+> **Description:** OCRmyPDF remains one of the most dependable open source building blocks for scanned PDF workflows. Its README describes a command-line tool that adds a searchable OCR text layer to image PDFs, which is exactly what legal archives, case files, and older scans often need before downstream AI can be trusted. It is not a glamorous “agent” repo, but it solves a very real prerequisite step and does it well. GitHub shows **32,014 stars**, **Python** as the primary language, an **MPL-2.0** license, and a **last commit date of December 15, 2025**.
