+#### [Layout Parser](https://github.com/Layout-Parser/layout-parser)
+> **Description:** Layout Parser’s README describes a unified toolkit for deep-learning-based document image analysis. The examples center on detecting regions, cropping them, sending them through OCR, visualizing layout boxes, and loading layout data from JSON, CSV, and PDFs. For lawyers and legal ops teams, that matters when extraction quality depends on page structure, not just text. It is especially useful for pleadings, forms, and exhibits where headers, sidebars, or tables can break naive OCR pipelines. GitHub shows **5,632 stars**, **Python** as the primary language, an **Apache-2.0** license, and a **last commit date of August 15, 2024**.
